 "traditions": [],
 "notes": "Air rifle and air pistol keep power sources as types and gain archetypes (Red Ryder, Daisy 25, Diana 27/34, Webley Service, HW 35/80/77/97, BSA Meteor, FWB 300/700, Walther LG, Daystate Huntsman, Air Arms S400, FX Impact; Crosman 1377). Red Ryder year left blank: Daisy Wikipedia says 1940, other sources say 1938. Air rifle models trimmed 20->12 (dropped JTS AirStryke, Macavity MA1/MA8, RTI Mora II, Umarex Komplete/Notos, Diana Bandit Tactical, Air Venturi Alpha); air pistol 23->14. Crosman 2240 kept as a model (no retrieved page). New kind Airsoft gun (cross-link to Sports airsoft). Pellet maker 'FX' normalised to 'FX Airguns'. | Coordinator: Airsoft gun removed; its home is E2 (Sports), which holds the same kind with archetypes."
}